This uses the `CategoryBudget` and `BudgetError` from the lesson: `record` throws `.emptyTitle` for a blank title, `.nonPositiveAmount` for an amount of zero or less, and `.overLimit(by:)` when the new total would pass the limit. Predict everything the loop prints.

```swift
var food = CategoryBudget(limit: 50)
let attempts: [(String, Decimal)] = [("Lunch", 12), ("", 5), ("Dinner", 45)]

for (title, amount) in attempts {
    do {
        try food.record(title: title, amount: amount)
        print("Saved \(title)")
    } catch BudgetError.overLimit(let by) {
        print("Over by \(by)")
    } catch {
        print("Rejected: \(error)")
    }
}
print(food.spent)
```
